From b8e33383f3e28e3bf10391b11e4401df98e26ebf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Security <marco@securityreviewer.net>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 16:51:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SCA Windows: make auditpol checks independent of the OS
 language

The CIS Windows policies checked audit settings with
`auditpol /get /subcategory:"<English name>" -> r:Success and Failure`,
which fails on any non-English Windows because subcategory names and
the output text are localized (e.g. Italian "Accesso" / "Esito positivo
e negativo"). "PNP Activity" and "Audit Other Object Access Events" were
not valid auditpol names even on English Windows.

Rewrite only the command of those rules (27-34 per policy, 8 policies):
run `auditpol /backup` to a temp CSV, pick the row by subcategory GUID and
map its numeric "Setting Value" column (0/1/2/3, language independent) to
the English strings the existing regexes expect. The `-> r:` part is
unchanged, so check semantics are the same.

Generated with decisionreviewer/scripts/sca_localize_auditpol_rules.py
(idempotent, re-run after syncing the upstream policies). Verified on an
Italian Windows 11 host: 27 rules run, 22 pass, 5 fail only because those
subcategories were genuinely not enabled. Not yet tested on ES/DE Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
